# Verification Checklist — Configure Identity Providers Lab

---

## Part 1 — SAML/WS-Fed IdP Federation ✅

- [ ] Navigated to **Identity → External Identities → All identity providers**
- [ ] Selected **+ New SAML/WS-Fed IdP**
- [ ] Entered the partner's domain namespace
- [ ] Selected the correct protocol (SAML 2.0 or WS-Fed)
- [ ] Provided required attributes (via metadata URL or manual entry)
- [ ] Saved the federation configuration
- [ ] Understood that existing guests are NOT affected by new federation setup
- [ ] Understood that deleting federation breaks existing guest sign-in

---

## Part 2 — Google Federation ✅

- [ ] Created a new project in **Google Developers Console**
- [ ] Configured the **OAuth consent screen** (External, added microsoftonline.com)
- [ ] Created **OAuth client credentials** (Web application type)
- [ ] Added both authorized redirect URIs:
  - `https://login.microsoftonline.com`
  - `https://login.microsoftonline.com/te/<tenant-ID>/oauth2/authresp`
- [ ] Copied the **Client ID** and **Client Secret**
- [ ] Configured Google federation in **Azure portal → Entra ID → External Identities**
- [ ] Entered Client ID and Client Secret → Saved
- [ ] Tested by inviting a Gmail address and accepting the invitation

---

## Part 3 — Facebook Federation ✅

- [ ] Created a new app in **Facebook Developers Console**
- [ ] Configured basic settings (category, site URL, privacy policy URL)
- [ ] Copied the **App ID** and **App Secret**
- [ ] Configured **Facebook Login** with the correct OAuth redirect URI
- [ ] Made the app **Live** (switched from Development to Live mode)
- [ ] Configured Facebook federation in **Azure portal → Entra ID → External Identities**
- [ ] Entered App ID and App Secret → Saved

---

## Exam-Style Questions — Test Your Understanding

**Q1: A partner organisation uses AD FS as their identity provider. Which federation type should you configure in Microsoft Entra ID?**
> **SAML/WS-Fed IdP federation** (also called direct federation). AD FS supports
> WS-Federation and SAML 2.0. You would configure the federation using the partner's
> AD FS metadata URL or by manually entering the required WS-Fed attributes.

**Q2: You configure Google federation after 50 guest users from Gmail have already redeemed their invitations. Will those guests now authenticate via Google federation?**
> No. Setting up federation does NOT change the authentication method for guests
> who have already redeemed their invitations. Those 50 guests continue using
> their original authentication method. To migrate them to Google federation,
> you must reset each user's **redemption status**.

**Q3: A user wants to sign up for your application using their Facebook account. Is this possible with B2B invitations?**
> No. Facebook federation is only supported for **self-service sign-up user flows**.
> Users cannot be invited via B2B and redeem their invitation using a Facebook account.
> To use Facebook, you must enable self-service sign-up and add Facebook as an
> identity provider in a user flow.

**Q4: You delete Google federation from your tenant. What happens to existing Google guest users?**
> Existing Google guest users who already redeemed their invitations will no longer
> be able to sign in. To restore their access, you must delete their guest account
> from the directory and reinvite them.

**Q5: What two authorized redirect URIs must be added when creating Google OAuth credentials for Entra B2B?**
> 1. `https://login.microsoftonline.com`
> 2. `https://login.microsoftonline.com/te/<your-tenant-ID>/oauth2/authresp`

**Q6: What is the difference between Google federation and configuring federation with a Google Workspace (G Suite) domain?**
> **Google federation** is for individual **Gmail users** (personal @gmail.com accounts)
> signing in as B2B guests. For **Google Workspace / G Suite** organisations with
> their own managed domain (e.g. @company.com powered by Google), you should use
> **SAML/WS-Fed direct federation** instead, as Google Workspace supports SAML.

**Q7: A Facebook app is in Development mode. Can regular users sign up with it?**
> No. While in Development mode, only Facebook developer accounts registered in
> the app can use it. The app must be switched to **Live** mode before regular
> users can sign up through it.

**Q8: Which two claims are required in the SAML 2.0 token issued by a federated IdP?**
> 1. **NameID Format** — `urn:oasis:names:tc:SAML:2.0:nameid-format:persistent`
> 2. **emailaddress** — `https://schemas.xmlsoap.org/ws/2005/05/identity/claims/emailaddress`

